1. PURPOSE
The OneDraft CI/CD, Build & Release Engineering subsystem provides the controlled mechanism by which source code becomes a tested, versioned, deployable and reproducible OneDraft software release.
The system shall automate:
source validation
dependency installation
static analysis
type checking
unit testing
integration testing
contract testing
database migration verification
geometry testing
documentation generation testing
container image construction
artifact generation
security scanning
release packaging
deployment
deployment verification
rollback
The objective is to ensure that no software change reaches a production environment without passing the required engineering gates.

2. CORE PRINCIPLE
OneDraft shall treat software releases as controlled computational artifacts.
The fundamental pipeline is:
SOURCE
 ↓
VALIDATE
 ↓
BUILD
 ↓
TEST
 ↓
SCAN
 ↓
PACKAGE
 ↓
VERSION
 ↓
PUBLISH
 ↓
DEPLOY
 ↓
VERIFY
 ↓
RELEASE
A failed stage shall prevent promotion to the next protected environment.

3. RELEASE ENGINEERING BOUNDARY
CI/CD is responsible for transforming source into deployable artifacts.
It is not responsible for making domain decisions.
The boundary is:
DEVELOPER
    ↓
SOURCE CONTROL
    ↓
CI PIPELINE
    ↓
BUILD ARTIFACT
    ↓
TEST / VALIDATION
    ↓
RELEASE ARTIFACT
    ↓
DEPLOYMENT SYSTEM
    ↓
RUNTIME
The runtime system remains responsible for executing OneDraft.
The CI/CD system remains responsible for proving that the runtime artifact is suitable for deployment.

