7. TEST ENVIRONMENT
The test environment shall provide deterministic automated testing.
It shall contain:
test PostgreSQL
test object storage
test queue
test workers
test API
test geometry services
test documentation services
Production customer data shall never be used as uncontrolled test fixtures.

8. STAGING ENVIRONMENT
Staging shall represent the production architecture as closely as practical.
The staging environment is the final deployment gate before production.
It shall execute:
database migration tests
integration tests
end-to-end tests
security checks
artifact verification
deployment verification
rollback verification

9. PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT
Production shall contain only release artifacts that have passed the required release gates.
Production deployment shall require:
successful build
successful tests
successful security checks
approved release
validated artifact
successful deployment
successful health checks

10. SOURCE CONTROL
The OneDraft repository shall be the authoritative source for application code, infrastructure definitions, migrations, tests and release configuration.
The repository shall contain, conceptually:
apps/
packages/
services/
workers/
migrations/
tests/
docs/
infra/
scripts/
.github/
Generated artifacts shall not replace source-controlled definitions.

11. BRANCH STRATEGY
The initial branch structure shall support:
main
develop
feature/*
release/*
hotfix/*
The precise branching strategy may evolve.
The protected production branch shall require successful automated checks before merge.

12. PULL REQUEST VALIDATION
Every pull request affecting executable software should trigger automated validation.
The minimum sequence is:
CHECKOUT
 ↓
INSTALL
 ↓
LINT
 ↓
TYPE CHECK
 ↓
UNIT TEST
 ↓
BUILD
 ↓
CONTRACT TEST
Additional tests shall execute when affected components require them.

13. CHANGE DETECTION
The pipeline should identify affected components where practical.
For example:
frontend change
    → frontend tests

API change
    → API tests
    → contract tests

geometry change
    → geometry tests
    → model tests
    → regression tests

database migration
    → migration tests
    → integration tests
Critical integration suites shall still execute for protected branches.

14. DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT
Dependencies shall be explicitly versioned.
The repository shall maintain lock files for supported package ecosystems.
Dependencies shall be:
pinned
auditable
repeatable
upgradeable
Dependency changes shall be included in CI validation.

15. PYTHON BUILD
Python services shall support deterministic dependency installation.
The build system shall validate:
Python version
dependency lock
package metadata
type compatibility
import integrity
test execution
The resulting Python application artifact shall be suitable for containerization.

16. TYPESCRIPT BUILD
Frontend and TypeScript packages shall validate:
