API client generation
production bundle
Generated API clients shall be derived from the authoritative OpenAPI contract.

17. DATABASE MIGRATION PIPELINE
Every PostgreSQL migration shall be tested before deployment.
The migration process shall be:
CREATE DATABASE
 ↓
APPLY ALL MIGRATIONS
 ↓
VERIFY SCHEMA
 ↓
RUN INTEGRATION TESTS
 ↓
DESTROY TEST DATABASE
Production migrations shall never be tested first against production.

18. MIGRATION ORDER
Migrations remain sequential and immutable.
For example:
001_initial_schema
002_identity
003_projects
...
032_release_metadata
A migration that has been applied to a shared environment shall not be modified in place.
A correction requires a new migration.

19. MIGRATION SAFETY
Production migrations shall be evaluated for:
locking
execution duration
data transformation
rollback requirements
backward compatibility
application compatibility
Large migrations should use expand-and-contract techniques where required.

20. DATABASE COMPATIBILITY
Application deployments must account for the relationship between:
APPLICATION VERSION
DATABASE VERSION
The deployment process shall prevent an application from requiring database structures that do not yet exist.
The preferred sequence is:
BACKWARD-COMPATIBLE DATABASE CHANGE
 ↓
APPLICATION DEPLOYMENT
 ↓
DATABASE FINALIZATION

