50. ROLLBACK
A failed deployment shall support rollback to the last known-good release.
Conceptually:
NEW RELEASE
 ↓
HEALTH FAILURE
 ↓
STOP PROMOTION
 ↓
RESTORE PREVIOUS ARTIFACT
 ↓
VERIFY
Rollback shall not rely on rebuilding the previous version.
The previous immutable artifact shall remain available.

51. DATABASE ROLLBACK
Database rollback shall be handled independently from application rollback.
Not every database migration is safely reversible.
Where destructive migration is involved, the release process must provide a tested recovery strategy.

52. FEATURE FLAGS
Feature flags may be used to separate:
deployment
from:
feature activation
This allows new functionality to be deployed without immediately exposing it to all users.
Feature flags shall themselves be versioned and auditable.

