Python version
Node version
package manager version
container tooling
database test version
Uncontrolled developer-machine dependencies shall not determine production builds.

64. PIPELINE CONFIGURATION
Pipeline definitions shall reside in source control.
For example:
.github/workflows/
or the equivalent CI platform configuration.
Pipeline changes shall undergo the same review discipline as application code.

65. BUILD SECRETS
CI secrets shall be provided through the CI secret-management mechanism.
The pipeline shall never print secrets to logs.
Logs shall redact sensitive values.

66. ENVIRONMENT PROMOTION
Promotion shall move the same immutable artifact between environments.
Preferred model:
BUILD ONCE
 ↓
TEST
 ↓
PROMOTE
 ↓
PROMOTE
 ↓
PROMOTE
The artifact should not be rebuilt separately for production.

67. CONFIGURATION PROMOTION
Application artifacts remain identical across environments.
Environment-specific behavior comes from controlled configuration.
Thus:
SAME ARTIFACT
+
DIFFERENT CONFIGURATION
=
DIFFERENT ENVIRONMENT

68. DEPLOYMENT ORDER
A multi-service OneDraft deployment should use an explicit dependency-aware order.
Conceptually:
